might recommend Candidate A.\n\nWe need to reference discussion: none, but we can say \"Given the current evidence, I propose...\" That's okay.\n\nWe must include explicit facts: e.g., \"Candidate A can anticipate dangerous situations and has very good leadership qualities, which support operational reliability and decision quality. However, they are regarded as a show\u2011off and not open to new ideas, which raises concerns about crew cooperation and adaptability.\"\n\nThen vote for Candidate A.\n\nProceed."}
