ift vote? But we need to make a focused argumentative contribution. Could we propose to probe other candidates? We could say we still support A but note concerns and request info on B's crew cooperation, etc. That would be a contribution.\n\nWe must include explicit candidate facts as evidence. Provide recommendation (vote). We can keep vote Candidate A, but note concerns. Or we could change vote if we think concerns outweigh. Let's evaluate: Candidate A's concerns: not good at taking criticism, unorganized, show-off, not open to new ideas. Those affect reliability, crew cooperation, adaptability. Candidate B: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at weather, excellent computer skills, but can be grumpy and uncooperative. That's also crew cooperation issue. Candidate C: quick decisions, calm, technical, but difficulty communicating, egocentric, not willing to further education. Also crew cooperation issues. Candidate D: responds to unexpected events, concentration, problem solving, responsibility, but arrogant, weak leadership. Also crew cooperation issues.\n\nAll have concerns. Which candidate has least severe? Hard to decide. Maybe we should ask for more info on stress resilience for A, and crew cooperation for B, C, D. But we need to produce a public message now. We can say: \"I agree with previous votes for A, but we still need to address concerns about his ability to take criticism and organization, which could affect reliability. I propose we ask Agent 2 about B's crew cooperation and Agent 3 about D's stress handling.\" However tool calls are separate; we can ask via tool. But we can also just state our recommendation and note need for more info.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: agree with A, highlight concerns, propose next steps. METADATA_JSON vote Candidate A.\n\nProceed."}
